                "username": "ifel"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_cable_message_registry.hpp",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't look like it's modeled correctly in Redfish.  I'd expect this would normally be a \"ResourceCreated\" message (when the cable object was created).\n\nWas this discussed with DMTF somewhere?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_cable_message_registry.hpp",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "This is what comes from the PDI repo and not what my code changes. I think if it does not look right, it should be discussed and corrected in PDI repo."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This looks like it's intending to create LOTS of registries.  There's no reason to take on the registry overhead if a registry isn't optional.  Just put them all into one registry until we find individual functions that need to be optional (and have code to do that)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe this was also covered when Patrick and I discussed this design initially."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The PDI design is a registry per events.yaml file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "We shouldn\u2019t be checking these in here (nor the generated header files) anyhow. We should be [optionally] depending on the results from PDI and dynamically building these. If we check this code in it is going to be out of date."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "The reason behind I checking these in, is, to have these accessible. But it seems the PublicationUri is optional in the code https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/6b0d0c1751208a09e0be300a52c82925547cdfe8/redfish-core/lib/message_registries.hpp#L120-L123 and spec https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/MessageRegistryFile.v1_1_0.json, so I will remove checking the jsons and use null URIs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group.json",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "I spoke with Patrick and confirmed that it had been designed this way."
                }
            ],
