            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/dbus_registries_map.hpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Doesn't look used in this commit?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/dbus_registries_map.hpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "It was an attempt to save some bytes by stripping a common prefix, and use it in the code, maybe it should've been added to another header, but I'm dropping this, and going to store full names to avoid confusions and additional operations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/dbus_registries_map.hpp",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Message Ids by convention are CamelCase"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/dbus_registries_map.hpp",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not a message ID, this is a DBus message name suffix (without \"xyz.openbmc_project.\")"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_logging_message_registry.hpp",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Mentioned this on the previous commit, but if these are now coming from PDI, we can't check them in as a fixed header anymore, we need to generate them at build time with something like a meson custom target or generator.\n\nThe whole point of PDI is to have one \"source of truth\" for what is allowed.\n\nPS, please implement the subproject wrap file when you do this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/registries/openbmc_state_leak_detector_group_message_registry.hpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This registry looks like it's a copy of the DMTF registry (It's too similar to not be a coincidence). Given the rules we have in OEM_SCHEMAS.md, we try not to duplicate things that have already been standardized.\n\nIn your other commit you Reved the environmental registry to one that had this define in it, so it's not clear what your intent is there.\n\nThoughts?"
                }
            ],
